    "description": "<p>As part of the US Department of Energy's Modern Grid Initiative, a set of prototypical electrical distribution feeder models were developed. These feeder models were based on 575 distribution utility models that were collected by the project team and using statistical clustering analysis, were generalized into 24 prototypical models based on the region of the country, the voltage class of the feeder, and the customer types served by the feeder. Though the feeder models used are proprietary, the published generalized models are not and contain no specific proprietary utility information. These models are saved in the GridLAB-D format.</p>",
